# NOTE: vsce applies negations (!) *last*, whatever the order — a `!out/**/*.js`
# rule would re-include the compiled tests no matter where it sits. So the
# compiled output is included by simply not excluding it, and negations are used
# only where something above genuinely has to be undone.

# Sources and tooling — the package ships compiled JS only.
.vscode/**
.github/**
src/**
**/*.ts
**/*.map
tsconfig.json
node_modules/**
package-lock.json

# Compiled tests, their harness, and the lint configuration
out/test/**
scripts/**
.vscode-test.mjs
.vscode-test/**
.eslintrc.json
.prettierrc.json
.prettierignore

# VCS and build artifacts
.git/**
.gitignore
.gitattributes
*.vsix
*.zip

# Repo-only documentation (README.md, LICENSE and CHANGELOG.md are shipped)
#
# Matched by *pattern*, not by name. These were listed individually, and the next
# review document — REVIEW_2026-08-09.md — was therefore packaged: 375 KB of
# internal notes quoting the source verbatim, with absolute paths from the author's
# machine and a worked reproduction of every unfixed defect, published to the
# Marketplace. Anything named REVIEW* stays out by construction now.
REVIEW*.md
REVIEW*/**
PUBLISHING.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
# The long-form companion to the README — public, but repository-only. Shipping it
# would be dead weight: vsce rewrites every relative link in the packaged README to
# the repository URL, so the "Full reference" link resolves against GitHub whether
# or not the file is in the .vsix.
REFERENCE.md

# Local dev/runtime state — must never ship in the package
.claude/**
# The bare name matches only the root copy; macOS leaves one in every directory.
**/.DS_Store
